### Feedback API - IntelliJ HTTP Client
### Run the Spring Boot app, then click the green run icon beside any request.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### ============================================================================
### VALID FEEDBACK SUBMISSIONS
### ============================================================================

### 1. Submit feedback - Valid inquiry
POST {{baseUrl}}/feedback
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "type": "inquiry",
  "subject": "Question about subscription plans",
  "message": "I would like to know more about the premium features and pricing options available for students."
}

###

### 2. Submit feedback - Valid feedback
POST {{baseUrl}}/feedback
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "Jane Smith",
  "email": "jane.smith@example.com",
  "type": "feedback",
  "subject": "Great platform!",
  "message": "I love using iStudy for my studies. The practice questions are very helpful and the interface is user-friendly."
}

###

### 3. Submit feedback - Valid support request
POST {{baseUrl}}/feedback
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "Mike Johnson",
  "email": "mike.j@example.com",
  "type": "support",
  "subject": "Login issue",
  "message": "I am having trouble logging into my account. I keep getting an error message saying 'Invalid credentials' even though I'm sure my password is correct."
}

###

### 4. Submit feedback - Valid other type
POST {{baseUrl}}/feedback
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "Sarah Williams",
  "email": "sarah.w@example.com",
  "type": "other",
  "subject": "Partnership opportunity",
  "message": "I represent an educational institution and would like to discuss a potential partnership with iStudy for our students."
}

###

### 5. Submit feedback - Long message
POST {{baseUrl}}/feedback
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "David Brown",
  "email": "david.brown@example.com",
  "type": "feedback",
  "subject": "Detailed feedback on the platform",
  "message": "I have been using iStudy for the past three months and wanted to share my detailed feedback. The platform has been incredibly helpful for my exam preparation. The question bank is comprehensive and covers all topics thoroughly. However, I would suggest adding more video explanations for complex topics. The progress tracking feature is excellent and helps me identify my weak areas. The mobile app works smoothly and I can practice on the go. Overall, I'm very satisfied with the service and would recommend it to other students. Keep up the great work!"
}

###

### ============================================================================
### VALIDATION ERROR TESTS
### ============================================================================

### 6. Submit feedback - Missing name (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/feedback
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "type": "inquiry",
  "subject": "Test subject",
  "message": "This should fail because name is missing."
}

###

### 7. Submit feedback - Invalid email format (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/feedback
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": "invalid-email",
  "type": "inquiry",
  "subject": "Test subject",
  "message": "This should fail because email format is invalid."
}

###

### 8. Submit feedback - Empty email (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/feedback
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": "",
  "type": "inquiry",
  "subject": "Test subject",
  "message": "This should fail because email is empty."
}

###

### 9. Submit feedback - Invalid type (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/feedback
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "type": "invalid_type",
  "subject": "Test subject",
  "message": "This should fail because type is invalid."
